TrueNAS controller authentication and connection ownership
=========================================================

The saved-controller connection check maps the decrypted password field to
TrueNAS API-key authentication, matching onboarding and storage operations.
Legacy plaintext and encrypted stored credentials are accepted consistently;
wrong keys remain rejected and tenant checks run before authentication.

TrueNASAdapter.connect reuses its already-open transport instead of replacing
an unclosed WebSocket or HTTP client. A standalone test_connection closes the
transport even when system-info retrieval fails. Sequential reconnect after
explicit disconnect still works. This is not a concurrent connection lock or
an automatic reconnect policy after network failure.

Qualification uses actual adapters and authentication serialization, with
synthetic appliance responses. The dedicated before/after probe additionally
uses PostgreSQL, HTTP-ASGI and a real loopback TLS WebSocket connection with a
probe CA. Identity, quota, appliance response and discovery publication edges
are synthetic. It does not qualify a new TrueNAS version or modify hardware.
Existing direct adapter username/password authentication and unrelated Omada
cloud/Proxmox API-token parameter handling remain supported.
